build a team if you want to have success  as an entrepreneur you need to build a  team you need to build beyond yourself  because you cannot do everything  yourself and you shouldn't be doing  everything yourself one of my favorite  stories is about Ben &amp; Jerry's ice cream  they were founded by two friends Ben and  Jerry who in 1977 decided hey we want to  get into the food business these guys  were lifelong friends and they thought  the bagel business was too expensive so  they said okay let's go into the ice  cream business and they spent five  dollars to get this correspondence  course on how to make ice cream and so  they set up shop they learn how to make  ice cream they invested eight thousand  dollars of their own money in four  thousand dollars and borrowed money they  took over this this you know ghetto gas  station and started Ben &amp; Jerry's ice  cream the problem was they started  losing money these guys were were the  prototypical entrepreneur doing  everything themselves making the product  driving the truck doing the sales and  marketing balancing the books everything  and they realized we're not great with  numbers we suck at numbers we're not  good at this and we're losing money and  they had to put a sign up on their door  to close down the shop one day to say  we're closed because we're trying to  figure out what's going on talk about  being authentic and it started to change  when I realized hey we're not good at  the numbers we shouldn't be focusing on  this if it if this company depended on  us knowing our numbers and this being  our core competency we're going to fail  so they brought on somebody to help them  they had a friend who was a local  nightclub owner named Fred lager who  came on board he became their first coo  and the company started to turn around  he watched the books he did all the  numbers he handle all the money and the  company finally started to make a profit  and it helped put the company on track  to what it is now a global brand with  tons of sales but it may not have ever  gotten there at Ben and Jerry tried to  do it all themselves and this is the  important lesson for you as a business  owner you can't do everything yourself  there's there's so much that you have to  do to run a business and this is this is  why it's hard this is why so many  companies so many entrepreneurs  shut down because there's so much stuff  that you have to do and you end up  spending so much time doing the stuff  that you hate doing the stuff that  you're not good at that you spend so  little time on the stuff that it's  actually high-value where you're the  expert and you want to focus as much  time on that I call that CEO time as  much time on that as possible and not  all the other crap that still needs to  get done but shouldn't you get shouldn't  shouldn't be being done by you so  whether that's bringing on somebody  part-time full-time as an employee as a  consultant as a partner in the business  your business will never be great as  long as you are doing things that you  are not great at does that make sense  you want to focus on what you're really  good at what you love doing where you  had tons of value where you really help  people where you know by doing this you  could change the world and everything  else should be given to other people who  are greater that and let them run with  it that's how you build a quality  organization you have to start building  a team and stop trying to do everything  yourself believe for those you watching  I love to hear what you have to think  I'd love to hear how you're trying to  build your team up leave it in the  comments below or ask me a question in  the comments below you can click on the  link in the description to support me in  these videos give the video a thumbs up  click on my face subscribe to the  channel thank you so much I'll see you  soon
 

